From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:15:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw-hdmi: allocate the bridge with
 devm_drm_bridge_alloc

WIP/1000 "drm/rockchip: dw-hdmi: add bridge and switch to
drm_bridge_funcs" embeds a struct drm_bridge in struct rockchip_hdmi and
sets bridge.funcs by hand, but the container is still obtained with
devm_kzalloc(). Bridges are reference counted now and have to come from
devm_drm_bridge_alloc(), which is what sets ->container and takes the
first reference.

Because neither is initialised, every boot logs:

  [drm] DRM bridge corrupted or not allocated by devm_drm_bridge_alloc()
  refcount_t: addition on 0; use-after-free.
  WARNING: lib/refcount.c:25 at refcount_warn_saturate
   drm_bridge_attach
   dw_hdmi_rockchip_bind

and then, when the first bind defers and unwinds, the matching:

  refcount_t: underflow; use-after-free.
  WARNING: lib/refcount.c:28 at refcount_warn_saturate
   drm_bridge_put
   drm_bridge_detach
   drm_encoder_cleanup

Allocate the container with devm_drm_bridge_alloc() and drop the manual
funcs assignment, which the allocator now does.

Tested on a Radxa ROCK Pi N10 (rk3399pro): the three warnings are gone.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -750,9 +750,10 @@
 	if (!np)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	hdmi = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*hdmi), GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!hdmi)
-		return -ENOMEM;
+	hdmi = devm_drm_bridge_alloc(&pdev->dev, struct rockchip_hdmi, bridge,
+					     &dw_hdmi_rockchip_bridge_funcs);
+	if (IS_ERR(hdmi))
+		return PTR_ERR(hdmi);
 
 	match = of_match_node(dw_hdmi_rockchip_dt_ids, np);
 	plat_data = devm_kmemdup(&pdev->dev, match->data,
@@ -816,7 +817,6 @@
 		goto err_disable_clk;
 	}
 
-	hdmi->bridge.funcs = &dw_hdmi_rockchip_bridge_funcs;
 	drm_bridge_attach(encoder, &hdmi->bridge, NULL, 0);
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, hdmi);
-- 
2.53.0
